[01:53.60] The holts are nearly always close to the sea
[01:56.54] In fallen boulders, old ruins, in cliffs
[02:00.60] Or at the top of a stack, like this
[02:02.78] High above the sea
[02:04.44] A safe place for cubs
[02:08.94] I wait, tense
[02:08.94] Then disappointed
[02:13.12] She leaves her spraint
[02:14.72] To notify others have a visit
[02:36.50] The holts are evenly spaced
[02:41.06] About five hundred yards apart
[02:43.38] And are for the use of any otter who passes by
[02:47.18] With or without cubs
[02:48.92] I love you
